"""Register the ForceProjector absorbExplosion rows (N2423).

N2235 ported the updateTile advance -- but absorbExplosion
(ForceBuild.absorbExplosion(), ForceProjector.java:269-277) is
a SEPARATE method (the ExplosionShield interface,
ForceProjector.java:164, called from explosion handling:
Damage.explode, Damage.java:113, and the unit crash path,
UnitComp.java:906 -- NOT from updateTile), so it stayed
deferred as DEFERRED #148. N2423 ports it as a pure with
explicit inputs (broken, ex, ey, damage, sides, building x/y,
real_radius, shield_rotation, the current hit, and
crash_damage_multiplier defaulting to 2f): absorb is !broken
&& the explosion point inside the regular polygon at the real
radius (the N2235 isInRegularPolygon port, REUSED -- no second
polygon test), hit is set to 1f only when absorb (reported as
hit_value + a hit_set flag, so the caller can tell "set to 1f"
from "already 1f"), and buildup grows by damage *
crashDamageMultiplier (2f, ForceProjector.java:45) only when
absorb. The absorbEffect.at FX defers (the N2235 effects
precedent) under its own narrow entry.

Scoping (from real Java, no guesses): (1) the gate is
`boolean absorb = !broken &&
Intersector.isInRegularPolygon(sides, x, y, realRadius(),
shieldRotation, ex, ey);` (ForceProjector.java:270) -- the
SAME polygon test deflectBullets uses
(ForceProjector.java:61), so the pure calls the N2235 helper
instead of porting it twice. (2) Java sets hit to 1f ONLY
when absorb (:273) and grows buildup by damage *
crashDamageMultiplier ONLY when absorb (:274); when the gate
is false Java touches neither field. So the pure reports
hit_value (1f on absorb, the incoming hit otherwise) PLUS a
hit_set flag (true only on absorb) -- without the flag a hit
already at 1f would be indistinguishable from a fresh set.
(3) real_radius is an EXPLICIT input: the caller supplies
the N2235 advance's real_radius result ((radius + phaseHeat *
phaseRadiusBoost) * radscl, ForceProjector.java:280), so the
pure does not re-derive it. (4) crashDamageMultiplier is the
class value 2f (ForceProjector.java:45) -- the def does not
override it (Blocks.java:1964-1976) -- carried as a driver
constant and an explicit pure param defaulting to it, so a
proof can still vary it. (5) there is NO tick wiring:
absorbExplosion is called from Damage.explode
(Damage.java:113, `s.absorbExplosion(x, y, damagePerWave)`)
and the unit crash path (UnitComp.java:906,
`s.absorbExplosion(x, y, crashDamage)`), never from
updateTile -- pure-only, like the draw rows. (6) the
absorbEffect.at call (:272, `public Effect absorbEffect =
Fx.absorb;`, ForceProjector.java:49) is FX: it defers under
its own narrow entry and is not modeled. (7) the zero-damage
edge: the gate never checks damage, so a 0-damage explosion
inside the polygon still absorbs and still sets hit, with a
buildup delta of 0. Shard note: the defense shards DO change
-- defense_slices.json and defense_api_contracts.json each
gain the N2423 entry (pure additions, no other shard):
defense_slices selects ledger rows whose java_source is under
/world/blocks/defense/ (this slice's ForceProjector.java
qualifies, as N2217/N2218/N2230/N2235 already do at HEAD),
and defense_api_contracts mirrors the contracts of those
owners.
"""

